OL,3,GNEWSAReform UK councillor claims 'grass
OL,4,Adoes not grow'                         
OL,6,FA Reform UK councillor has questioned  
OL,7,Fwhy a council has bought a new fleet of
OL,8,Flawnmowers, claiming that grass is no  
OL,9,Flonger growing due to climate change.  
OL,11,FAngela Baker, who represents Keighley  
OL,12,FEast, made the comments at Bradford    
OL,13,FCouncil's Keighley Area Committee      
OL,14,Fmeeting after being told the           
OL,15,F10-year-old mowers were being replaced 
OL,16,Fwith new ride-on John Deere models.    
OL,18,FCatherine Smith, head of parks and     
OL,19,Fstreet cleansing services, said grassed
OL,20,Fareas were usually cut 10 times a year 
OL,21,Fbut this had reduced to seven in 2026  
OL,22,Fdue to droughts and heatwaves.         
OL,23,APub: 26-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2 
